 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "A timeout or latency cascade is unlikely. No service has a p95 latency onset, p95 stays at or below 140ms, and failing traces complete in 9-84ms, so these are fast failures, not slow ones.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-03f01a29eb0b",
    "ev-4081415f77fb",
    "ev-e960c3ed491b",
    "ev-fdffab1af452"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Gateway and orders are not the origin. Their errors only report the downstream status (orders returned 502; inventory returned 500), and inventory is the deepest failing span.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-bf38338a2a0a",
    "ev-668d724aaa57",
    "ev-fdffab1af452"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Which peer is resetting inventory's connections (database, cache, or another dependency)? There is no evidence from that dependency.",
  "No deployment records are in the snapshot. It is unknown whether inventory 3.1.5, or any other change, was rolled out shortly before 08:19:37Z.",
  "There are no infrastructure metrics for inventory or its backend (connection pool usage, restarts, network) to explain the resets.",
  "Gateway's error ratio (max 39.3%) is lower than orders/inventory (56.5%). This presumably reflects non-checkout gateway traffic, but that is not confirmed."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Inspect inventory's outbound dependencies for POST /reserve (DB/cache health, connection pool, restarts) around 08:19:37Z, and pull the example traces 96b56f065ccbfcabc554ab013d50c263 and b740f27878e327ad556818c07b9fb6cb to identify the peer.",
   "rationale": "Inventory is where the errors originate, and its logs show connection resets to an unidentified peer.",
